betes and acromegaly. In 2005, the society published a monograph that outlined evidence-based nutritional recommendations, further emphasizing its commitment to advancing knowledge in these areas. Overall, the Sociedad Española de Endocrinología y Nutrición focuses on the study and treatment of endocrine disorders, contributing significantly to the healthcare landscape in Spain.", "HO PJ ET AL.:Ho PJ et al. conducted research on the regulation of pulsatile growth hormone secretion in normal subjects and patients with acromegaly.", "KATZNELSON L ET AL.:Katznelson L et al. provided clinical practice guidelines for acromegaly published in J Clin Endocrinol Metab in 2014.", "X-LAG:X-linked acrogigantism syndrome (X-LAG) is a condition characterized by early-onset gigantism due to genetic mutations.", "ADENOMA HIPOFISARIO SOMATOTROPO:", "CARDIOVASCULAR DISEASE:Cardiovascular disease refers to a group of disorders affecting the heart and blood vessels. This condition encompasses a range of ailments that can be influenced by various factors, particularly dietary and lifestyle choices. Key dietary factors linked to cardiovascular disease include fat and sodium intake, as well as fiber and omega-3 fatty acids. Additionally, obesity and diabetes are significant risk factors associated with the prevalence of cardiovascular disease.\n\nThe condition can be exacerbated by testosterone treatment and is often discussed in relation to metabolic health. It is also noted that cardiovascular disease is associated with increased mortality in patients with acromegaly. Preventative measures for cardiovascular disease can include dietary modifications, such as adopting low-fat diets like the Ornish and Pritikin diets.\n\nOverall, cardiovascular disease is a complex health issue that is influenced by a combination of dietary habits, lifestyle factors, and underlying health conditions, making it a critical area of study and intervention in public health.", "HORMONAL DISORDERS:Hormonal disorders refer to conditions that result from an imbalance in hormone levels, which can lead to various health issues, including acromegaly.", "MUTACIONES ACTIVANTES:Activating mutations are genetic changes that lead to increased activity of certain proteins, such as those involved in hormone production, and are often implicated in conditions like acromegaly.", "HIPERPLASIA:Hyperplasia refers to the increase in the number of cells in an organ or tissue, which can lead to overproduction of hormones, including growth hormone in the context of acromegaly.", "SÍNDROME DE MCCUNE-ALBRIGHT:McCune-Albright syndrome is a genetic disorder characterized by fibrous dysplasia of bone, skin pigmentation, and precocious puberty, often associated with hormonal imbalances.", "MACROADENOMAS:", "MELMED S.:Melmed S. is a prominent researcher and author recognized for his significant contributions to the understanding of acromegaly, including its causes and clinical manifestations. He is notably an author and editor of the Williams Textbook of Endocrinology, which serves as a key reference in the field of endocrinology. Through his work, Melmed S. has made substantial contributions to academic literature, enhancing the knowledge and understanding of endocrine disorders.", "KATZNELSON L.:Katznelson L. is a researcher and author who has contributed to the understanding of acromegaly and its treatment."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}